# A fix is not done until you've asked "where else does this live?"

OWEN parses four input languages, and it parses each of them in **several
independent places**. The same lexing primitives — comment stripping, line
continuation, token/keyword tables — are **re-implemented per consumer**, not
shared. So a bug is almost never confined to the one file where it was reported.

When you fix any parsing, lexing, diagnostic, geometry, or convention bug, do the
two sweeps below **before** you report the fix. Record the result (even if the
answer is "checked, not affected") in the changelog entry for the fix.

## Sweep 1 — same bug, other layers of the *same* language

Find every place that re-implements the primitive you just touched and apply the
same fix (or extract a shared helper). Known duplication as of Nov 2026:

**MCNP line handling** (continuation = blank cols 1–5 or prev line ends `&`;
`$`/`c` comments; surface-mnemonic table) is duplicated in:
- `src/preview/codes/mcnp.ts` — `leadingColumns`, `logicalCards`, `SURFACE_MNEMONICS`
- `src/converter/mcnpModel.ts` — `stripComment`, `joinContinuationLines`
- `src/language/rules.ts` — the linter card loop
- `packages/mcnp-workspace/src/mcnpReferences.ts` — cross-reference / undefined-surface index
- `src/preview/mcnpGeometry.ts`

Frank Helk's Nov 2026 reports (false "undefined surface", wrong material-sign from a
`$` comment) were a **direct result** of these copies drifting apart. All five now
agree on the continuation rule (tab-aware, ≥5 blank columns or trailing `&`), the
comment rule, and the mnemonic table — `mcnpModel.ts` was the last straggler (it used
a non-tab-aware `≥4 spaces` test). They are still five copies; a shared MCNP lexer is
the proper fix and remains outstanding.

**Serpent** input comments (`%` to EOL + C-style `/* */` blocks that may span lines,
per `serpent.tmLanguage.json`; **no `#`**) are now stripped by one shared helper,
`src/preview/commentStrip.ts::stripSerpentComments`, used by both
`src/preview/codes/serpent.ts` and `src/preview/serpentGeometry.ts`. Before Nov 2026
these had drifted: the fast extractor only stripped single-line `/* */`, and the
geometry parser additionally (wrongly) stripped `#`. The Serpent **results** reader
`src/results/parsers/serpent.ts` parses MATLAB-format `_res.m` output (quote-aware
`%`, no blocks) — a different grammar; it keeps its own stripper and must NOT use the
shared one.

**SCONE** input comments (`//` and `!` to EOL, per `scone.tmLanguage.json`; **no block
comment**) are now stripped by `stripSconeComments`, used by both
`src/preview/codes/scone.ts` and `src/preview/sconeGeometry.ts`. Before, the fast
extractor wrongly stripped `/* */` (not a SCONE comment) while the geometry parser did
not.

**OpenMC** is XML + Python, not column/comment lexing, but still parsed in more than
one place (`src/language/openmcXml.ts`, `src/preview/codes/openmc.ts`,
`src/preview/openmcNative/*`); check them together for XML/attribute bugs.

If the same logic now exists in 3+ copies, prefer **extracting a shared per-language
helper** (as `src/preview/commentStrip.ts` now does for Serpent and SCONE comments)
over fixing N copies again. That is the real cure; mirroring is the stopgap.

## Sweep 2 — same *class* of bug, the other three languages

Ask whether the analogous construct in the other codes has the same defect. The four
languages solve the same problems with different syntax, so a convention bug in one is
usually latent in the others. Examples of parallel constructs:

- **Comment forms:** MCNP `$`/`c`, Serpent `%` + `/* */`, SCONE `//`/`!` (no block
  comment), OpenMC XML comments. A "comment not stripped before reading numbers" bug
  applies to all.
- **Per-primitive preview metadata** (`CylinderSpec.cell`/`universe`, component,
  material): a 3D scene comes from five builders — the four `src/preview/codes/*.ts`
  fast paths and the shared `csgScene.ts` — plus helpers that emit shapes for them
  (`palette.ts emitLayers`, `radialStructure.ts`, `openmcShells.ts`). A new field is
  not done until every one of them sets it; `src/test/suite/previewCells.test.ts`
  covers one deck per language and the CSG path.
- **Line continuation / token joining:** MCNP cols 1–5 + `&`; Serpent whitespace tokens
  across lines; SCONE brace blocks; OpenMC XML nesting.
- **Keyword/type tables being incomplete** (the missing MCNP cone/point-pair surfaces):
  check Serpent surface types, SCONE surface/universe keywords, OpenMC element names.
- **Sign / unit conventions** (MCNP density & fraction signs): each code has its own —
  verify the fix didn't assume MCNP semantics elsewhere.

## What "done" requires

1. Fix applied to **every** sibling copy found in Sweep 1 (or a shared helper extracted).
2. Sweep 2 performed; any same-class defect in another language either fixed or filed.
3. A test that reproduces the original report (prefer the reporter's real deck), plus a
   test for each sibling copy you touched.
4. A changelog line that states the root cause and the cross-layer / cross-language
   result — not just "fixed X". If a sweep found nothing, say "swept, not affected".
5. Reporter credited per `.cursor/rules/owen-semver.mdc` when the fix ships.
